# §22.5 #8a wilderness-priest-banish: pin the dungeon-context cast of
# priest banish via path 2 (earthquake bridge). Two priests in slots
# 1+2 (seed 2 wi 67/63 — both qualify for banish at lv 5: at lv 5
# wi += 4*8 → 99/95, ma reset to wi). Slot 1 casts earthquake (cost
# 60 at lv 5 = 99 → 39) which spawns a cave + dives into a 5..18-
# level dungeon; on dungeon level 1 the random fill happens to roll
# `gold` (id 2 — "You find 132 gold pieces."), whose wait_input the
# .in absorbs. Slot 2 then casts banish (cost 90 at lv 5: ma 95 → 5)
# inside the dungeon — the success arm runs the six-screen
# incantation, ends with the state_banished mutate, and back in
# dungeon.c the post-spell `if (state.banished)` zeroes out every
# lvl[i] in 3..5 across the dungeon.
#
# Snapshot caveat — slot 2 ends with ma=6, not 5. Earthquake's
# advance_hour beat fires foodhandler which runs the 50% mana_regen
# roll over slot 2 (priest, ma<wi); on this seed it lands and bumps
# ma by 1 between cost-debit and snapshot. The pinned post-cast
# value would be 5 if banish ran without the regen tick; the +1
# from regen is observable behaviour, not a bug.
#
# Pinned: state.banished = 1 after the cast (snapshot), banish-arm
# narration emitted, both priests' ma debits applied (slot 1 ma=39
# post-earthquake, slot 2 ma=6 = 95-90+1 post-regen). Unpinned by
# this fixture: the not_in_dungeon arm (place != 1), the not_enough_
# pts arm.
RYL_FAKE_EPOCH=1700000000
RYL_FAKE_SEED=2
RYL_NO_DELAY=1
RYL_FORCE_PARTY_LV=5
